# 20. Feature Importance

Decision Trees can estimate how useful features were for splitting.

```python
for feature, importance in zip(
    iris.feature_names,
    model.feature_importances_
):
    print(feature, importance)
```

A higher importance generally indicates that the feature contributed more to reducing the chosen split criterion across the tree.

⚠️ Important interview point: impurity-based feature importance can be biased in some situations, especially with certain high-cardinality features.

